<article class="env-lemma" id="0AIA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AIA">Lemma <span data-tag="0AIA">87.9.4</span>.</a> Let $X_\lambda , \lambda \in \Lambda $ and $X = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits X_\lambda $ be as in Definition <a href="/tag/0AI7" data-tag="0AI7">87.9.1</a>. If $Y$ is a quasi-compact algebraic space over $S$, then any morphism $Y \to X$ factors through an $X_\lambda $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose an affine scheme $V$ and a surjective étale morphism $V \to Y$. The composition $V \to Y \to X$ factors through $X_\lambda $ for some $\lambda $ by the discussion following Definition <a href="/tag/0AI7" data-tag="0AI7">87.9.1</a>. Since $V \to Y$ is a surjection of sheaves, we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>